# Jay Panchal portfolio — project context

Personal portfolio for Jay Panchal (Business Analyst @ Neome.ai, Ahmedabad). Single-page React app.
Jay runs and edits this project in **Cursor**, from `~/Documents/GitHub/Jay-Panchal-BA` (the copy whose
dev server is on localhost:3000). A second clone of the same repo exists at `~/Projects/Jay-Panchal-BA`
(used by Claude Code sessions) — the Cursor copy is the source of truth; changes made in the other
clone must be copied here. Keep this file up to date when you make notable changes (new sections,
new conventions, new gotchas) so every future chat starts with the right context.

> `README.md` is outdated (old component list, wrong port/path). Trust this file over it.

## Run it

- `npm install` (Node 18+)
- `npm run dev` → **http://localhost:3000** (`strictPort: true` in `vite.config.ts`; if 3000 is busy the
  server fails instead of picking another port — stop the other process)
- `npm run build` → `tsc -b && vite build` (always run before calling work done; it type-checks)
- `npm run playlists:sync` → refresh Spotify playlist songs + covers (see "On rotation" below)

## Stack

React 19 + TypeScript (strict, `verbatimModuleSyntax`, no `resolveJsonModule` → use `.ts` data files,
not `.json` imports) · Vite 8 in the Cursor copy (the other clone is still on Vite 5) · Tailwind v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`) but the landing page is mostly plain
CSS · `motion` (`motion/react`) for animation · `lucide-react` + `@tabler/icons-react` icons · `cobe` globe.

