## Design conventions

- Geist / Geist Mono (`--font-geist`, `--font-geist-mono`).
- **Landing = bento grid** (`bx-*`, max 1080px): boxes of different sizes share 1px hairlines — the boxes
  sit on a `.bx-lines` layer and the 1px grid gaps show it through. Lines stay inside the column; only short
  crop marks run into the gutters (≥1200px). "+" marks sit where lines cross (pseudo-elements on rows/boxes).
  **No cards inside boxes** (Jay's explicit rule): content sits straight on the box, with a mono
  `01 — LABEL` in the top-left corner (`BoxLabel`). Inner hairlines between list items are fine.
- Motion: on load the lines draw in top-down (`bx-draw`, clip-path), then "+" marks pop and crop marks grow;
  box content fades up (first screen on `ready`, the rest on scroll). A neutral cursor spotlight brightens
  lines near the pointer (`--mx/--my` set in `Bento`, fine pointers only). All off under reduced motion.
- Header is 1080px wide on home (no rule; hairline appears once scrolled); the floating dock only shows
  after scrolling past the first screen on home.
- Sub-pages (Work/About): narrow lined column (`.gx-col`, max 768px), full-bleed rules, hatched separators,
  "cards within cards" (`.gx-card`) — older system, still in use there.
- Colour tokens in `globals.css` (`--ds-*`, `--bg`, `--text`, `--muted`, `--edge`, …).
  **Dark mode = `html.dark` class** (toggled by `useTheme`, saved in localStorage `jay-theme`) — not the
  OS media query. Every new style needs to work in dark mode (prefer tokens over hex).
- Mobile: ≤720px every bento box stacks full width (profile row keeps photo beside name; Impact stays 3-up;
  Connect becomes a row of 3 icons). Tablet tweaks ≤900px. The turntable uses a container query (520px).
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Match surrounding code: small focused components, short comments explaining *why*.
- Process: for big changes Jay wants a grill-me style discussion first (numbered questions with a
  recommended answer each), and building starts only once he confirms.

## "On rotation" — Spotify turntable (`src/components/home/Playlists.tsx`)

Recreates a vinyl-turntable UI (from a reference screen recording) for Jay's 3 Spotify playlists:
Alive 🕊️ (`72PKk905OzSzSog1N8OLmC`, 402 songs), Mastana 💛 (`3GTTRXXSnKGdzmz6DuVlPp`, 306),
Gujju Rocks (`6JmjJn7Ex6aZ3TppK4yMf2`, 54).

### Playback — own audio engine, NOT the Spotify embed
- `src/lib/turntableAudio.ts` (`TurntableAudio`) plays Spotify's official **30-second preview clips**
  (`https://p.scdn.co/mp3-preview/<id>`) in one `<audio>` element, through a Web Audio graph
  (gain + analyser). The Spotify iFrame embed was removed on Oct 16, 2026: logged-out visitors got
  a "Get Spotify" pop-up that paused playback after a few plays, and its async state made
  play/pause drift ("plays when I want it stopped"). Don't bring the embed back.
- **`engine.wantsPlay` is the single source of truth** for "playing". It flips instantly on a
  command; the UI reads it via `useSyncExternalStore(engine.subscribe, () => engine.version)`.
  Never derive play state from audio events or timers.
- Vinyl touches: play starts the element silently inside the click (Safari needs that), the tonearm
  swings over for `ARM_TRAVEL_MS`, then sound lands with a pitch spin-up (`playbackRate` 0.5→1,
  `preservesPitch = false`), a synthetic needle crackle, a ripple and an arm wobble. Pause winds
  down (rate sags, gain fades) then pauses. All skipped under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Play order (Oct 17, Jay's choice):** each record starts on its pinned song (`startsWith` in
  `src/data/playlists.ts`: Mastana → Tere Vaaste, Gujju Rocks → Garba Shuffle), then shuffles with no
  repeats until every song has played (`newShuffle` / `stepShuffle` / `jumpShuffle` in `Playlists.tsx`).
  Prev walks back through what was heard; a tracklist pick plays and shuffle carries on after it.
  Alive starts on "295" by Sidhu Moose Wala (the song is *named* 295). It's beyond the 100 songs the
  public embed gives us, so it's added by hand via `extraTracks` in `playlists.ts` (data taken from the
  song's own public embed page; the sync script doesn't touch it). Jay declined Spotify API credentials,
  so add any other "deep" song the same way.
- Previews are always Spotify's own 30s clips. Apple Music's clips were tried for "295" (Oct 17) and
  Jay preferred Spotify's — don't switch preview sources again unless he asks.
- Full songs: Jay chose to keep 30s previews (full songs for every visitor aren't possible legally);
  a "Full song on Spotify ↗" link (`.pl-full`) sits next to the Tracklist toggle.
- Songs auto-advance (`onEnded` → next); failing clips are skipped (stops after 3 in a row).
  Prev restarts the song if >3s in. Media Session API wires lock-screen/media keys.
- Keyboard while focus is inside the stage: Space = play/pause, ←/→ = previous/next.
- Spotify's embed data only exposes each playlist's **first 100 songs** — those are what can play.
  The real totals (`PLAYLIST_TOTALS`) are shown ("100 of 402 songs"). Getting all songs would need
  Spotify Web API credentials.

### UI
- Layout: left record · deck (platter + tonearm) · right record; details + pill player
  (play · time · live waveform · total · prev/next) + status line + collapsible **Tracklist**
  (every playable song with art; tap to play; scrolls to the current song).
  Mobile (container ≤520px): deck, details, then the two other records in a row.
- Interactions: drag the tonearm onto the vinyl → play from that groove; release it anywhere off the
  vinyl, or after swinging it past the label (`overshotRef`), → lift/pause. A window `pointerup` +
  `onLostPointerCapture` make sure a drag always ends (Oct 17 fix: song kept playing after a drop) (angles are normalised to 0–2π so swinging past the pivot never "drops" on the
  run-out groove). Drag the progress ring or waveform to scrub. Click a side record → records swap
  (motion `layoutId`); if music was on, the arm lifts, swaps, and the new record starts.
- Each record shows the **album art of its current song** (`trackArt(p, track, 64|300|640)`), the
  side records keep the last song played on them. The playlist cover is only a fallback.
- Glow: album colour is sampled from the art (canvas; Spotify's CDN allows CORS) into `--pl-glow`;
  `--pl-energy` pulses with bass *beats* (level above its running average), driving a halo under the
  platter (`.pl-glow`) and a stage wash (`.pl-stage.is-playing::before`).
- Waveform bars are `scaleY`-animated from the analyser (per-bar running max so quiet songs move too).
- Spin is deliberately slow: `SPIN_DEG_PER_S = 30` (one turn per 12s) — Jay asked for "very slow".
  Skips give the platter a quick flick (`impulseRef`).
- Geometry is in "record units" (disc radius 100, platter centre = origin, `VIEWBOX`).
  `needleAngleFor(r)` / `needlePoint(angle)` convert between tonearm angle and groove position.
- All per-frame animation runs in one `requestAnimationFrame` loop writing to refs/DOM — don't move
  it into React state.

### Data
- Edit names / genre labels ("mood") / covers in `src/data/playlists.ts`. After changing songs on
  Spotify (or adding a playlist), run `npm run playlists:sync` (`scripts/sync-playlists.mjs`): it
  regenerates `src/data/playlistTracks.ts` — per song `[trackId, title, artists, durationMs, artId,
  previewId]` — plus `PLAYLIST_TOTALS`, and the fallback covers. Rate-limit safe; reuses known art.

### Gotchas
- In SVG, CSS variables don't work reliably in presentation attributes (`fill="var(--x)"`) — use
  `style={{ fill: 'var(--x)' }}` or a CSS class.
- Testing in a hidden/background browser pane: rAF drops to ~2fps, so animations look laggy there.
  Judge motion in a visible tab.

